{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for MCP implementation exact2db9160b97e1f48ddab18d7d36c193e3e9fe9d31/treec4f7f8f1205bdd4f47ae98b9dae5957dc10ab4e8, against approved D7 plan031. Primary delivery note first; all59 artifacts reviewed within the coverage qualifications below.\n\n[P1] Preserve uncertainty and newest settlement in custody (custody.ts196–255). Refused→explicit resubmit→lost/unavailable preserves terminal refused; settle then returns without a native read, concealing possible later acceptance. Persist an unresolved attempt BEFORE resending, retaining old refusal as history. Accepted/mismatch must stay retained rather than resubmitted. Also ordinary send prefers ANY historical answer over a newer settled receipt: lost→unavailable→settled accepted returns stale unavailable. Choose the latest chronological outcome across both forms. Add both exact sequences with no replacement envelope/key.\n\n[P1] Make archive/index publication atomic across identities/processes (node.ts67–123). Per-record locks do not protect the shared archive/index. Two processes can append from the same observed offset, rewrite divergent index snapshots and delete both live records; the last index rewrite loses the other's lookup. archive also moves records whose locks it does not own. Use a coordinated archive/index transaction or lease respecting record ownership, publish durable indexed data before deletion, and make interrupted segment append/record rewrite idempotent. Witness distinct-identity cross-process concurrency and crash boundaries; same-process/same-key and sequential tests are insufficient.\n\n[P1] Complete MCP-only onboarding required by W1 (inventory.ts35–39; CLI mcp adapter; room story47). A nonmember cannot discover/call room.join without repository/membership pin configuration. The story injects these through ConfigPort; delivery explicitly requires artroom join first and says MCP reads no pins from the directory. Provide the authorized MCP invitation/room configuration path with persisted validated identity/pins and fresh-home enrollment/unknown recovery. Do not declare this complete by requiring another interface.\n\n[P2] Coordinate capacity and byte-aware spilling (custody.ts152–188). Separate key locks allow two admissions at255 unresolved to exceed256. Spill-by64-outcomes ignores the2MiB record cap: a valid envelope/receipt can exceed it AFTER submission, losing durable definitive outcome. Reserve shared capacity, budget bytes before retaining, and preserve every act outcome through indexed spill/archive. Test concurrent distinct keys and large allowed envelope/receipt combinations. Clarify step-history retention; do not silently transfer act-history proofs to the64-step truncation.\n\n[P2] Recover locks after expiry (node.ts101). A settlement acquired after envelope expiry writes held.time\u003e=notAfter; stale-lock recovery permanently requires the opposite even after PID death. Permit safe post-expiry recovery without treating expiry as outcome, and witness process death during that settlement.\n\n[P2] Refresh semantic/config state after remembering a room or inbox (service.ts144,755–766). #remember writes configuration but #current keeps its old snapshot. Generic create/found/wait/actions therefore cannot resolve the newly created membership until a gratuitous room/tools-list refresh. The story calls names before every step and masks it. Refresh/invalidate at the relevant write/call boundary; prove immediate membership/seat/key actions after wait and discovery of externally changed roots.\n\n[P2] Apply budgets to whole client-visible results and all orientation collections (service.ts81,430–462,517,559; paging.ts14). Text and structuredContent duplicate JSON, so60/64KiB slices exceed the64KiB whole-response requirement. room pages lanes but not roots/standing/active/hidden collections and can exceed8KiB without continuation. Preserve all lawful data through bounded continuations and the specified whole-large-item exception; test actual serialized responses rather than doubling limits. Segmented history lookup also reads unbounded files: retain positional/bounded access as designed.\n\n[P2] Progress native history searches (service.ts699–724,783). Final-item wait ignores next after the first page. Creation and credential search only the next63 entries, restarting the same window each call. Real completed work beyond either boundary becomes permanently invisible. Use necessary native continuations/resumable causal searches with bounded per-call work and witnesses beyond both cutoffs.\n\n[P2] Bind descriptions/generation to rendered rule/profile meaning (catalogue.ts105–136,218–231; describe.ts287–291). Same act/item types but different named-rule bodies collapse to one first-holder description; sorted representative pin can disagree with that holder, and scope reorder changes prose without generation change. Preserve native identity while rendering per-pin differences or a specified meaning binding, and include all rendering dependencies in semantic generation. No native authorization bypass is claimed. Prefix variants already extend8hex at a time correctly; no fixed-prefix collision finding.\n\n[P2] Describe actual authority and complete inputs (catalogue.ts159–160; describe.ts102,318,476–479). Known-lacks plus unknown standing is labelled mixed and says a known grant holds somewhere; keep unknown tools reachable without inventing that grant. Presented-fact schema omits named/required facts even while prose points there; derive properties/required/closed constraints. Capability range prose drops except, changing the required set. Add semantic assertions for each case, not merely absence of raw JSON. Existing shapePresented remains a native-shape fence.\n\n[P2] Preserve HTTP bytes and contain invalid frames (node.ts185,215–220; wire.ts66). Per-chunk UTF8 decoding corrupts split multibyte fields before signing. Decode bounded bytes once/statefully. null/scalars reach revision classification before frame guard, and discarded async handler failures can hang/unhandled-reject. Validate before classification, return bounded errors, contain abort/parser/handler failures and prove a subsequent healthy SDK call.\n\n[P2] Own subscriptions and bound the long-lived transport (wire.ts152–207; node.ts143–160,209,225). Global modern listeners keyed only by JSONRPCid collide when independent clients each use listen:0; cancel/disconnect can affect the other listener. Bind IDs/lifecycle to actual client/stream ownership. IncomingMessage.close denotes request completion, not response/socket lifetime; use the correct SSE closure signal. Prune resolved stdio tasks and bound incomplete line/frame bytes without truncating valid envelopes. Witness equal-ID clients, abrupt disconnect/reconnect, watcher cleanup and sustained stdio traffic. [Node HTTP lifecycle](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#class-httpincomingmessage).\n\n[P2] Correct evidence/docs and finish owning witnesses. docs/mcp.md1124 wrongly says propose-file content detached; native change.ts837 declares plain inline text. Correct it. W1 label/tool census is not executed argument-complete recipes. W2 room story has no review and no accepted foreign-resource preparation, and does not assert the exact capability-refused/not-staged reason its note claims; accepted retry is scripted. Supply the full owned W1–W7 evidence without erasing those limits. Budget observations assert counts for only the last of70 refusals, average list-page size, and no warm credential success after cold consumption; strengthen the appropriate witnesses/labels. Real pinned SDK clients are used for HTTP/stdio both revisions against a stand-in backend. The claim server2.3.1 is2025-only is false: its pinned README states2026-07-28 support. Correct the rationale; D7 still permits a minimal conformant handler. [Pinned server README](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/v2.3.1/packages/server/README.md).\n\nCurrent-main composition is required before a mergeable successor. Seven inherited Shell artifacts equal old approved1e52/base1086; Main/claim/sending/joined-shell/assets differ newer main, and wordmarks are now landed. Preserve current Empty/wordmark/Home/forms work; do not reinstall old inherited Page bytes.\n\nArchitecture: generic definition-driven tools and separate preparation custody are the right direction, but onboarding, semantic snapshots and bounded causal reads are incomplete. Security: strong loopback bearer/Origin fences are present; custody terminal truth, archive durability and transport ownership require repair. Simplification: one service can replace app-specific interfaces after these invariants hold; retain the complete adopted scope rather than shifting W1 work to CLI or shrinking data/history.\n\nValidation/limits:10676B primary FULL Root/peers. Six independent Source reviews and all finals/audits FULL Root; native unit hashes/LF/EOF, changed units and59-path coverage independently verified. New authored bodies FULL; commands/Main explicitly partial affected units/deltas; inherited shell authority exact; executable generated asset hash-only. ToolsJSON240097B reviewed as FULL lossless data-token projection, NOT rawBODYFULL:27000 raw prefix plus143892B token tape, all strings/escapes/numbers/order preserved,96205 outside-string whitespace bytes removed and complete mapping verified. Lock review covers all adopted changed data, not literal whole body. Root audit3119B SHA0f27681724a6759d65ebb469c814980e2df4523b92bde03d509c9654598032d5. Truncated locator/three-unit probes receive zero authority and were bounded-recovered.\n\nNo checker Source/test/gate/install/browser/provider/live-MCP/private log/credential/program execution or reads. Cloud gate4checkers failures retained. Planner reports local1077PASS2SKIP2timeouts, isolated edit pass/baseline Git push failure and unassigned fixture exception; no CLOSED local gate projection has been read, no green final gate or inferred root cause. Gate-pass condition/W1–W7 remain unmet. Prepare binds dd024/7012→main; no approval/landing/hosted/native/parent acceptance. Stage2 and other explicitly owed outcomes remain owned; estimates only sequence full scope.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fec75a9f34a4ce68e2f8dcba1242edda05841506","binding":"assigned","head":"2db9160b97e1f48ddab18d7d36c193e3e9fe9d31","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9261f4100eb353f999a2fe45d039083cd0be8ffb\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7012ef651c9b5c26807bf4679bde8811eb686fac\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cb479790fceb4d0d98b17e2546a003a5ee5d0dab","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}